                                                                  2025 1451
Ca-40 resolved resonance parameter evaluation was perfomed in the 2025 1451
energy range from 1e-5 eV to 1.5 MeV with the SAMMY code[ref1].   2025 1451
Two capture and five transmission measurements for natural Ca-40  2025 1451
natural tungsten were included in the evaluation:                 2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
nat-Ca Cierjacks (transmission) 500 keV up to 1.5 MeV [ref2]      2025 1451
nat-Ca Perey     (transmission) 200 keV up to 1.5 MeV [ref3]      2025 1451
40 -Ca Johnson   (transmission)  40 keV up to 1.5 MeV [ref4]      2025 1451
nat-Ca Singh     (transmission)   2 keV up to 500 keV [ref5]      2025 1451
nat-Ca Guber     (transmission)   0 keV up to 900 keV [ref6]      2025 1451
nat-Ca Guber     (capture thin)   0 keV up to 350 keV [ref6]      2025 1451
nat-Ca Guber     (capture     )   0 keV up to 350 keV [ref6]      2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
Resonance parameter covariance matrices were also obtained in     2025 1451
the SAMMY evaluation process in the energy region up to 1.5 MeV.  2025 1451
The RML formalism (LRF=7) was used for the resonance parameters   2025 1451
and the formalism (LCOMP=1) for the covariance matrix.            2025 1451
Thermal cross sections ( for reconstructed cross sections at      2025 1451
T=293.6 K ) are reported below                                    2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
