************** G E N E R A L   I N F O R M A T I O N *************2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
This evaluated data file is based primarily on a theoretical      2025 1451
analysis with the nuclear model code TALYS [kon04], version 0.56. 2025 1451
The nuclear model parameters of TALYS have been adjusted to       2025 1451
reproduce the existing experimental data. The resulting data file 2025 1451
provides a complete representation of nuclear data needed for     2025 1451
transport, damage, heating, radioactivity, and shielding          2025 1451
applications over the incident neutron energy range from          2025 1451
1.0E-11 to 200 MeV.                                               2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
This file is part of a larger collection of isotopic evaluations, 2025 1451
all created by running TALYS with input parameters that do not or 2025 1451
slightly deviate from the default values. The mutual quality of   2025 1451
these isotopic evaluations is thus relatively consistent.         2025 1451
The same set of nuclear models is used and, equally important,    2025 1451
the same ENDF-6 formatting procedures for each isotope. We have   2025 1451
intended to make this evaluation complete in its description of   2025 1451
reaction channels, and use a compact method to store the data.    2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
For certain reactions and energy ranges TALYS may not be used.    2025 1451
This is the case when TALYS is not appropriate, such as for the   2025 1451
description of resonances, or when the directly available         2025 1451
experimental data is of better quality, as for e.g. low-energy    2025 1451
total cross sections. In these cases, we have adopted the best    2025 1451
possible data from an existing library, or directly from unfiled  2025 1451
experimental data. All transport data for particles, photons and  2025 1451
residual nuclides are filed using a combination of MF1,2,3,4 and  2025 1451
MF6. This includes cross sections, angular distributions,         2025 1451
double-differential spectra, discrete and continuum photon        2025 1451
production cross sections, and residual production (activation)   2025 1451
cross sections. Moreover, isomeric production data are stored in  2025 1451
MF8 and MF10. This evaluation can thus be used as both transport  2025 1451
and activation library. The data file has been created            2025 1451
automatically using the ENDF-6 format generator TEFAL.            2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
##### ORIGIN                                                      2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
Data < 200 MeV  : New evaluation NRG Petten                       2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
Resonance parameters (MF2/MT151): JENDL-3.3   for E < 500 keV     2025 1451
Total cross sections (MF3/MT1)  : ENDF/B-VI.8 for E < 20  MeV     2025 1451
All other data                  : Produced with TALYS code        2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
*************************** T H E O R Y **************************2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
TALYS is a computer code system for the prediction and analysis   2025 1451
of nuclear reactions. TALYS simulates reactions that involve      2025 1451
neutrons, gamma-rays, protons, deuterons, tritons, helions and    2025 1451
alpha-particles, in the 1 keV - 200 MeV energy range and for      2025 1451
target nuclides of mass 12 and heavier. This is achieved by       2025 1451
implementing a suite of nuclear reaction models into a single     2025 1451
code system. It enables to evaluate nuclear reactions from        2025 1451
the unresolved resonance region up to intermediate energies. This 2025 1451
evaluation is based on a theoretical analysis that utilizes the   2025 1451
optical model, compound nucleus statistical theory, direct        2025 1451
reactions and pre-equilibrium processes, in combination with      2025 1451
databases and models for nuclear structure. For Ca-40, the        2025 1451
following output of TALYS is stored in this data file:            2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
- Total, elastic and non-elastic cross sections                   2025 1451
- Elastic scattering angular distributions                        2025 1451
- Inelastic cross sections to discrete states                     2025 1451
- Inelastic scattering angular distributions to discrete states   2025 1451
- Exclusive channel cross sections, e.g. (n,g), (n,2n), (n,np),.. 2025 1451
- Exclusive channel energy spectra                                2025 1451
- Exclusive channel double-differential spectra                   2025 1451
- Exclusive gamma production for discrete states and continuum    2025 1451
- Isomeric and ground state cross sections                        2025 1451
- Residual production cross sections                              2025 1451
- Total particle cross sections, e.g. (n,xn), (n,xp),..           2025 1451
- Total particle energy spectra                                   2025 1451
- Total particle double-differential spectra                      2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
Here follows a short description of the used nuclear models:      2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
##### OPTICAL MODEL                                               2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
All optical model calculations are performed by ECIS-97 [ray94],  2025 1451
in TALYS used as a subroutine. The default optical model          2025 1451
potentials (OMP) used are the local and global parameterizations  2025 1451
of Koning and Delaroche [kon03]. These are phenomenological OMPs  2025 1451
for neutrons and protons which in principle are valid over the    2025 1451
1 keV - 200 MeV energy range, though the low energy boundary of   2025 1451
validity may differ from nucleus to nucleus (e.g. for the total   2025 1451
cross sections, experimental data are included directly in the    2025 1451
file for energies below that boundary). Solving the Schroedinger  2025 1451
equation with this OMP yields the total cross section, the        2025 1451
shape-elastic cross section, the shape-elastic angular            2025 1451
distribution, the wave functions for the direct reaction cross    2025 1451
sections (see below), the transmission coefficients for the       2025 1451
compound nucleus model (see below) and the reaction cross         2025 1451
sections for the pre-equilibrium model (see below).               2025 1451
For neutrons and protons, the used parameterization is given in   2025 1451
Eq. (7) of [kon03].                                               2025 1451
To calculate the transmission coefficients and reaction cross     2025 1451
sections for deuterons, tritons, helions and alpha particles, we  2025 1451
use OMPs that are directly derived from our nucleon potentials    2025 1451
using Watanabe's folding approach [mad88].                        2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
##### DIRECT REACTIONS                                            2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
The built-in ECIS-97 is used for coupled-channels or DWBA         2025 1451
calculations for rotational or vibrational (or a combination of   2025 1451
these) nuclides. For Ca-40, DWBA was used to compute the direct   2025 1451
cross sections to several low-lying discrete levels:              2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
Level   Energy  Spin/Parity   Deformation length delta_L          2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
   2   3.736690   3.0-          1.340                             2025 1451
   3   3.904380   2.0+          0.360                             2025 1451
   4   4.491430   5.0-          0.930                             2025 1451
 + a few additional states with small deformation parameters.     2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
In addition, a macroscopic, phenomenological model to describe    2025 1451
giant resonances in the inelastic channel is used. For each       2025 1451
multipolarity an energy weighted sum rule applies and a DWBA      2025 1451
calculation with ECIS-97 is performed for each giant resonance    2025 1451
state. The cross section is then spread over the continuum with a 2025 1451
Gaussian distribution.                                            2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
##### COMPOUND NUCLEUS                                            2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
For binary compound nucleus reactions we use the model of         2025 1451
Moldauer [mol80], i.e. the Hauser-Feshbach model [hau52]          2025 1451
corrected for width fluctuations. The transmission coefficients   2025 1451
have been generated with the aforementioned OMPs and the full     2025 1451
j,l-dependence of the transmission coefficients in the            2025 1451
Hauser-Feshbach model is used. For each nucleus that can be       2025 1451
reached through a binary reaction, several discrete levels and a  2025 1451
continuum described by level densities are included               2025 1451
simultaneously as competing channels.                             2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
The compound nucleus angular distributions are calculated with    2025 1451
the Blatt-Biedenharn formalism [bla52], leading to compound       2025 1451
nucleus Legendre coefficients that are added to their direct      2025 1451
counterparts. For multiple compound emission, i.e. emitted        2025 1451
particles after the binary emission, we use the Hauser-Feshbach   2025 1451
model. Again, for each residual nucleus several discrete states   2025 1451
are included as well as a continuum described by level densities. 2025 1451
Multiple compound emission is continued until all reaction        2025 1451
channels are closed and the population distribution of all        2025 1451
residual nuclides is depleted, through gamma decay, until they    2025 1451
end up in the ground state or in an isomer.                       2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
For the level density, we take the composite formula proposed by  2025 1451
Gilbert and Cameron [gil65], consisting of a constant temperature 2025 1451
law at low energies and a Fermi gas expression at high energies.  2025 1451
For the level density parameter a we use the energy dependent     2025 1451
expression proposed by Ignatyuk [ign75] to take into account the  2025 1451
damping of shell effects at high excitation energy. We have       2025 1451
obtained the parameters for the Ignatyuk formula from a           2025 1451
simultaneous fit to all experimental D_0 values as present in the 2025 1451
RIPL library. If necessary, we adjust individual parameters to    2025 1451
obtain a better fit to experiment.                                2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
Gamma-ray transmission coefficients are generated with the        2025 1451
Kopecky-Uhl generalized Lorentzian for strength                   2025 1451
functions [kop90], with giant dipole resonance parameters taken   2025 1451
from the RIPL library [rip98], and normalized with experimental   2025 1451
radiative widths [gar84].                                         2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
##### PRE-EQUILIBRIUM REACTIONS                                   2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
For pre-equilibrium reactions, which become important for         2025 1451
incident energies above about 10 MeV, we use the two-component    2025 1451
exciton model [kon04b], in which the neutron or proton types of   2025 1451
particles and holes are followed throughout the reaction. For     2025 1451
energies above 20 MeV, multiple pre-equilibrium emission up to    2025 1451
any order of particle emission was included in the calculations.  2025 1451
A parameterization for the squared matrix element is used that is 2025 1451
valid for the whole energy range of this evaluation.              2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
For deuterons, tritons, helions and alpha-particles, an extra     2025 1451
contribution was added from the pick/up and knock-out reaction    2025 1451
model by Kalbach [kal01].                                         2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
For photons, the model of Akkermans and Gruppelaar [akk85] was    2025 1451
applied, to simulate the direct and semi-direct capture           2025 1451
processes.                                                        2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
The angular distribution systematics by Kalbach [kal88] were used 2025 1451
to describe the angular distributions for all continuum           2025 1451
particles. An isotopic distribution for photons was adopted.      2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
****** C O M P A R I S O N    W I T H    E X P E R I M E N T *****2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
This evaluation was performed simultaneously with other adjacent  2025 1451
isotopes, both for incident neutrons and protons. This enables,   2025 1451
when compared with a single-isotope effort, to put stronger       2025 1451
constraints on the produced calculated data, i.e. a globally      2025 1451
good comparison between TALYS and experimental data is requested  2025 1451
for all isotopes at the same time, while nucleus-specific input   2025 1451
(default or adjusted) parameters are consistently used for all    2025 1451
isotopes. Also, experimental data that is not available for the   2025 1451
isotope under study may be present, and tested, for adjacent      2025 1451
nuclides or for other projectiles. If these can be successfully   2025 1451
described by the models, a similar performance can be expected    2025 1451
for the present data file.                                        2025 1451
A few level density parameters for residual nuclides have been    2025 1451
adjusted to enforce agreement with the experimental data. The     2025 1451
changes in the level density parameters, a, were all kept within  2025 1451
10% of their default values.                                      2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
##### TOTAL AND REACTION CROSS SECTIONS AND ELASTIC SCATTERING    2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
The spherical OMP was tested against experimental data for total  2025 1451
cross sections and elastic scattering angular distributions.      2025 1451
Consult [kon03] for the complete experimental database and for a  2025 1451
comparison of calculations and measurements over the whole energy 2025 1451
range.                                                            2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
##### INELASTIC CROSS SECTIONS                                    2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
For inelastic scattering to the level 1 [per70,smi94],            2025 1451
2 [per70,ols90], 3[per70], and 4 [per70,smi94,ols90], the         2025 1451
calculations have been tested against the available measurements. 2025 1451
They are also validated, for the first few MeV, with experimental 2025 1451
data on the specific gamma ray from the first, second and third   2025 1451
level to the ground state [bas66], produced by the (n,n')         2025 1451
reaction. No further renormalization was necessary to describe    2025 1451
the experiments. Inelastic scattering angular distributions for   2025 1451
the first 3-  and 5- states were tested against the available     2025 1451
data at 11 and 20 MeV [bai77] (reasonable fit, some               2025 1451
underestimation at forward angles).                               2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
##### OTHER PARTIAL CROSS SECTIONS                                2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
- (n,gamma):                                                      2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
The calculated capture cross section is renormalized, by          2025 1451
overruling the default renormalization to the s-wave strength     2025 1451
function, to the available experimental data, all taken from the  2025 1451
EXFOR database. A normalization factor of 0.50 was used. Further, 2025 1451
the E1 giant resonance energy was changed to 17 MeV to better     2025 1451
describe the direct/semi-direct peak around an incident energy    2025 1451
of 14 MeV. The pre-equilibrium gamma cross section was adjusted   2025 1451
to the data by multiplying the calculated result by a factor of   2025 1451
0.7.                                                              2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
- (n,2n):                                                         2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
The calculated results do not coincide at all with the single     2025 1451
experimental (n,2n) data set[arn65]. Independent GNASH and EMPIRE 2025 1451
calculations also suggest the data of [arn65] are too high.       2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
- (n,p):                                                          2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
Both experimental (n,p) cross sections for the first 4 discrete   2025 1451
final levels [bas66] and the total (n,p) cross sections           2025 1451
[ure61,all61] were used as validation.                            2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
- (n,a):                                                          2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
Validated with many experimental data from EXFOR.                 2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
##### PARTICLE SPECTRA                                            2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
For Ca-40, an adjustment of the default matrix element            2025 1451
parameterization of [kon04b] for pre-equilibrium reactions of a   2025 1451
factor of 0.7 was needed, to describe the aforementioned cross    2025 1451
sections and emission spectra for nuclides in this mass range.    2025 1451
For high-energy neutron and charged particle spectra, the average 2025 1451
quality is also determined by the pre-equilibrium model and its   2025 1451
global parameterization. No high-energy experiments are           2025 1451
available, though neutron induced reaction spectra between 28 and 2025 1451
63 MeV on Al [ben02], Si [ben02b] and Fe [sly03] have enabled us  2025 1451
to better constrain the results, through the aforementioned       2025 1451
matrix element, for particle yields and double-differential       2025 1451
spectra for all ejectiles up to alpha particles.                  2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
***************** F I L E   I N F O R M A T I O N ****************2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
##### MF1: GENERAL INFORMATION                                    2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
- MT451    : Descriptive data and directory                       2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
This text and the full directory of used MF/MT sections.          2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
##### MF2: RESONANCE PARAMETERS                                   2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
- MT151    : Resonance parameters                                 2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
Resolved parameters for MLBW formula were adopted from JENDL-3.3. 2025 1451
They are given in the energy  region from 1.0e-5 eV to 500 keV.   2025 1451
Parameters were taken from the recommended data of BNL [mug81]    2025 1451
and the data for a negative resonance were added so as to         2025 1451
reproduce the recommended thermal cross sections for capture and  2025 1451
scattering [mug81].  The scattering radius was assumed to be      2025 1451
3.6 fermi. Calculated 2200 m/sec cross sections and resonance     2025 1451
integrals are as follows:                                         2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
           2200 m/s cross section(b)     res. integral(b)         2025 1451
   elastic      3.022                                             2025 1451
   capture      0.408                       0.2125                2025 1451
   total        3.430                                             2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
##### MF3: REACTION CROSS SECTIONS                                2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
Unless stated otherwise, all the data present in the following    2025 1451
MT-sections have been calculated with TALYS. If the maximal cross 2025 1451
section in an excitation function over the whole energy range     2025 1451
does not exceed 1.e-9 b, the MT-number is not included at all.    2025 1451
Cross sections lower than 1.e-20 b are assumed to have no         2025 1451
physical meaning and are set to zero.                             2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
- MT1      : Total cross section                                  2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
Below 20 MeV, MT1 is adopted from ENDF/B-VI.8. The experimental   2025 1451
total cross sections from ORNL, NBS and Karlsruhe were used to    2025 1451
obtain the best average set. Above 20 MeV, calculations from      2025 1451
the spherical OMP, tuned to the data of [fin93], were used.       2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
- MT2      : Elastic scattering cross section                     2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
Obtained by subtracting the non-elastic cross section from the    2025 1451
total cross section. At energies below 20 MeV, the elastic        2025 1451
cross section is thus derived from evaluated experiment-based     2025 1451
total cross sections and optical model based non-elastic cross    2025 1451
sections. Below 500 keV, resonance parameters are used.           2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
- MT3      : Non-elastic cross section                            2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
Calculated with the optical model over the whole energy range.    2025 1451
The results have been validated with existing experimental        2025 1451
neutron reaction cross section data, all taken from the EXFOR     2025 1451
database. Below 500 keV, resonance parameters are used.           2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
- MT4      : Total inelastic cross section                        2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
Sum of MT=51-91.                                                  2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
- MT5      : (n,anything) cross section                           2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
For energies below 20 MeV, MT5 contains the lumped (n,gamma x)    2025 1451
cross section, where x may represent neutron, proton, deuteron,   2025 1451
triton, Helium-3 or alpha. Using the relative yields of MF6/MT5,  2025 1451
the (n,gamma n), (n,gamma p), ..., (n,gamma alpha) can be         2025 1451
recovered. These cross sections are relatively small. However,    2025 1451
addition of these cross sections, which can not be stored in any  2025 1451
other MT-number, ensures that the partial cross sections add up   2025 1451
to the non-elastic cross section. Above 20 MeV, MT5 contains the  2025 1451
total non-elastic cross section, with which the information of    2025 1451
MF6/MT5 can be combined to obtain particle production cross       2025 1451
sections and (double-)differential cross sections.                2025 1451
                                                                  2025 1451
- MT16     : (n,2n) cross section                                 2025 1451
- MT22     : (n,na) cross section                                 2025 1451
- MT28     : (n,np) cross section                                 2025 1451
- MT29     : (n,n2a) cross section                                2025 1451
- MT44     : (n,n2p) cross section                                2025 1451
- MT45     : (n,npa) cross section                                2025 1451
